          "explanation": "Harari emphasizes that other humans (including Neanderthals) had bigger brains, used tools, and communicated. The unique Sapiens leap was **fictive language** — the ability to talk about gods, spirits, nations, money, and other things with no physical existence. This shared imagination is what allowed large numbers of strangers to cooperate. Agriculture came 60,000 years later.",
