          "explanation": "Harari coins 'romantic consumerism' to describe how, after industrialization dismantled traditional family and community, the market repackaged sources of meaning (belonging, identity, ritual, love) as **things to buy**. Travel becomes 'finding yourself.' A new outfit becomes 'expressing your true self.' A subscription box becomes 'community.' These are real human needs being addressed through purchase — which both helps and traps. The system depends on us continuing to seek meaning through consumption.",
