          "explanation": "Graeber and Wengrow's 2021 book *The Dawn of Everything* argues that pre-agricultural human societies were far more varied than Harari (or Diamond, or Pinker) suggest. Some were egalitarian; some were hierarchical; some moved seasonally between modes. The 'noble savage' Harari critiques is real, but his own counter-image — small egalitarian bands of hunter-gatherers — is itself an oversimplification. Recent archaeology shows complex pre-agricultural cities, seasonal democracies, and elaborate hierarchies. The pre-agricultural world wasn't one thing.",
